aarch64 #23 milestone-1: in-guest host_info synthesis + CIDER_INGUEST_IPC flag (WIP, gated off).

Adds the dev flag CIDER_INGUEST_IPC (parsed from apple[] in mach_driver_init, OUTSIDE
the VARIANT_DYLD block so BOTH the dyld-loader copy and libsystem_kernel.dylib see it;
the guest's host_info runs through the dylib copy at libc init). When on,
mach_msg_overwrite_trap_impl serves host_info (id 200) fully in-guest: HOST_BASIC_INFO
and HOST_PRIORITY_INFO, flavor-checked, cpu/mem via sched_getaffinity/sysinfo (NOT
sysconf, which is itself host_info and would recurse), reply laid out to match the MIG
__Reply__host_info bytes exactly.

WIP, default OFF (flag-off is byte-identical baseline). Enabling it presently SIGTRAPs
the guest: a pure RPC-skip leaves ciderd's reply-port/thread state unestablished, which
a later guest op asserts on (proven: real RPC + synthesized bytes runs clean). The fix
is the in-guest reply-port/thread layer (docs/fully-without-ciderd.md, the port-table
design); the synthesis here is the verified reference it will sit on. On top of 0050.

